  "caption": "Quinn tried the 'squat like a toddler' challenge and felt a sharp pinch at the front of the ankle. Walking was fine, deep squats were not.\n\nWhen the ankle is stiff, often after an old sprain that was never fully rehabbed, tissue at the front of the joint can get squashed at the end of the bend.\n\nWhat often helps: knee-to-wall drills and calf stretches, calf raises and single-leg strength, tweaking squat depth, landings and kicking volume for a while, and regular balance work.\n\nIf your ankle swells, locks or gives way, or the pinch hangs around despite consistent rehab, get it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
